# Every text file is stored with LF, and checked out with LF, whatever the
# developer's core.autocrlf says. The repository has always held LF only; what
# varied was the working copies — a Windows checkout with autocrlf=true turned
# them CRLF, and files touched by different tools ended up mixed, which is what
# made patching them by exact string so fragile. Binary files are detected and
# left alone (text=auto).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts run inside the Linux container — a CRLF line ending on the
# shebang line makes the kernel look for "/bin/sh\r" and the script fails to
# start. Covered by the rule above; kept explicit because it is the one place a
# CRLF breaks the product rather than a diff.
*.sh text eol=lf
